SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Scholz: Bei Waffenlieferungen gemeinsam mit Nato und EU vorgehen","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-04-06","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw14-de-regierungsbefragung-886556","claim":"Scholz said the Bucha killings were war crimes, urged Russia to withdraw, and insisted Germany would act on weapons deliveries only jointly with NATO and the EU rather than taking a special role.","locator":"lines 738-752","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Bundestag record of the chancellor's remarks and the parliamentary summary.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Spring 2022 crisis response and escalation management.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["The page is parliamentary summary rather than full verbatim transcript.","Coordination can be prudent restraint or delay depending on benchmark."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.4","2B.6","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz sichert Ukraine weitere Unterstützung zu","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-05-19","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw20-de-regierungserklaerung-europaeischer-rat-894656","claim":"Scholz said Russia must not win the war, that Germany would continue military support in a considered and internationally coordinated way, that there would be no German solo moves, and that Germany would do nothing to make NATO a party to the war.","locator":"lines 736-739","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary parliamentary summary of the chancellor's government statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 support-and-restraint phase.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is self-justifying and does not prove effectiveness.","It leaves open criticism that caution slowed delivery."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz will 'Marshall-Plan' fur Wiederaufbau der Ukraine","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-06-22","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw25-de-regierungserklaerung-897774","claim":"Scholz called for a Marshall Plan for Ukraine, pledged continued massive support including weapons, and announced an international expert conference under Germany's G7 presidency to plan reconstruction and the European path for Ukraine.","locator":"lines 739-744","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Bundestag summary of the chancellor's government statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 postwar planning and allied coordination.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["Reconstruction planning is not the same as war termination.","The source is a government statement and may emphasize achievements."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz: Wir erleben eine Zeitenwende","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw08-sondersitzung-882198?enodia=eyJleHAiOjE2OTY0MTgwMTMsImNvbnRlbnQiOnRydWUsImF1ZCI6ImF1dGgiLCJIb3N0Ijoid3d3LmJ1bmRlc3RhZy5kZSIsIlNvdXJjZUlQIjoiNjYuMjQ5LjY0LjIzNCIsIkNvbmZpZ0lEIjoiOGRhZGNlMTI1ZmQyYzM5MzJiOTQzYjUyZTlkMmNkNjUwNTc1NGUxNjIyMTJhMmNlMWJiNWFmMTVjMGQ0YmJmZSJ9._1DDYF-BozQY4Lh6F5m83kVhHrdvBc5vrA86jTNAaTU%3D","claim":"Scholz justified sanctions on Russia, justified the decision to supply Ukraine with weapons, and announced an additional 100 billion euro special fund for the Bundeswehr as part of a national effort.","locator":"lines 805-807","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Bundestag summary of the chancellor's special-session address.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact onset of the 2022 war response.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["Support for Ukraine and defense spending can still be criticized as late or insufficient.","This is a wartime justification speech, not an outcome evaluation."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.3","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"German Bundestag, 20th electoral term, Resolution","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw08-sondersitzung-beschluss-englisch-883506","claim":"The Bundestag resolution said Germany stands firmly with Ukraine and welcomed the Federal Government's role in the EU, NATO, and G7 response, including sanctions and support for Ukraine's right of self-defense.","locator":"section I, points 1-2","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary parliamentary resolution text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate 2022 war reaction.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but attributable to the Scholz-led government coalition.","contrary_evidence":["Parliamentary support is not identical to personal executive action.","The resolution validates the response, not its long-term effectiveness."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"European Council conclusions, 24 February 2022","publisher":"Council of the European Union","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2022/02/24/european-council-conclusions-24-february-2022/","claim":"EU leaders condemned Russia's unprovoked and unjustified military aggression, called for an immediate end to military action and withdrawal from Ukraine, and demanded respect for international humanitarian law and an end to cyber-attacks and disinformation.","locator":"paragraphs 1-2","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary EU institutional conclusions adopted the day of the invasion.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact start of the 2022 war and Germany's EU response.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Scholz as a European Council participant.","contrary_evidence":["EU conclusions reflect collective member-state action.","They do not isolate Scholz's individual contribution."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's military aggression against Ukraine: fourth EU package of sectoral and individual measures","publisher":"Council of the European Union","publication_date":"2022-03-15","url":"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2022/03/15/russia-s-military-aggression-against-ukraine-fourth-eu-package-of-sectoral-and-individual-measures/","claim":"The Council adopted a fourth sanctions package targeting Russian state-owned enterprises, finance, dual-use exports, energy-sector investment, and key individuals linked to the war effort.","locator":"introductory paragraphs and bullet list","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary EU sanctions release with concrete legal measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Early-war sanction escalation in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to the Scholz-led German position within EU sanctions policy.","contrary_evidence":["Sanctions are collective EU action, not Scholz alone.","This does not show direct battlefield conduct."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's aggression against Ukraine: EU adopts sixth package of sanctions","publisher":"Council of the European Union","publication_date":"2022-06-03","url":"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2022/06/03/russia-s-aggression-against-ukraine-eu-adopts-sixth-package-of-sanctions/","claim":"The Council said Russia's continuing war of aggression and reported atrocities justified a sixth sanctions package that included an oil-import ban and further economic restrictions.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary EU sanctions release referencing atrocities and specific measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 escalation of lawful economic pressure.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Scholz's German role in EU policy.","contrary_evidence":["Collective sanctions do not prove Scholz's personal initiative.","Sanctions alone do not end the war."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"European Council conclusions on Ukraine, 30 May 2022","publisher":"Council of the European Union","publication_date":"2022-05-31","url":"https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2022/05/31/european-council-conclusions-on-ukraine-30-may-2022/","claim":"The European Council demanded immediate humanitarian access, safe passage for civilians, full respect for international humanitarian law including treatment of prisoners of war, accountability for Russia and Belarus, and support for Ukraine's reconstruction and energy security.","locator":"paragraphs 1, 4-6","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary European Council conclusions with explicit humanitarian and reconstruction measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 wartime governance and reconstruction planning.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Scholz as German chancellor participating in EU decision-making.","contrary_evidence":["Collective conclusions, not individual conduct.","The page does not test German implementation."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Fluchtlinge aus der Ukraine in Deutschland","publisher":"UNHCR Deutschland","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/de/fluechtlinge-aus-der-ukraine-deutschland","claim":"Germany registered more than one million people fleeing from Ukraine in 2022, most of whom received temporary protection under an EU mechanism.","locator":"opening paragraph","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNHCR country page summarizing verified refugee-registration data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 refugee-reception outcome.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Scholz's government response.","contrary_evidence":["Refugee numbers reflect war severity as well as Germany's response.","This does not distinguish federal from state/local execution."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Mid-Year Trends 2022","publisher":"UNHCR","publication_date":"2022-12-31","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/publications/mid-year-trends-2022","claim":"By mid-2022 Germany had become the third-largest hosting country for refugees worldwide, with 2.2 million refugees, reflecting the scale of the Ukraine displacement crisis and Germany's reception role.","locator":"section on refugee-hosting countries around lines 415-417","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"UNHCR mid-year statistical report with explicit ranked figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 humanitarian burden and reception posture.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Scholz's government.","contrary_evidence":["This is a statistical context source, not an executive-policy record.","High refugee numbers alone do not prove policy quality."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukrainian refugees from Moldova arrive via air bridge in Germany","publisher":"Euronews","publication_date":"2022-03-26","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/03/26/uk-ukraine-crisis-germany-refugees","claim":"Reuters reported that Germany promised to admit 2,500 Ukrainian refugees from Moldova and that Scholz said Germany had already recorded around 250,000 Ukrainian refugees at that point.","locator":"paragraphs 639-652","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting carried by Euronews with a direct quote from Scholz.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Early-war humanitarian response.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect personal attribution via Scholz's quoted statement.","contrary_evidence":["The operational details are shared with other German officials and EU partners.","Does not by itself measure longer-term integration success."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Scholz defends Germany's caution on sending heavy arms to Ukraine","publisher":"Euronews","publication_date":"2022-05-01","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/01/uk-ukraine-crisis-germany-scholz","claim":"Scholz rejected criticism over slow heavy-weapon deliveries, saying he preferred caution to hasty decisions and that Germany acted fast but in concert with partners.","locator":"paragraphs 654-661","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters interview reproduced by Euronews with direct quotes.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Spring 2022 escalation-management debate.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["Caution can be prudent or unduly slow depending on baseline.","The article itself notes heavy pressure to move faster."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin will not dictate Ukraine peace terms: Scholz","publisher":"Euronews","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/27/us-davos-meeting-scholz","claim":"Scholz said there would be no dictated peace, that Ukraine would not accept one, and that Russia would only negotiate seriously once it accepted it could not win the war.","locator":"paragraphs 669-676","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report quoting Scholz directly at Davos.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 peace-process positioning.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["The article notes he did not address heavier arms requests in that passage.","This supports peace posture but not a completed settlement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Germany's Scholz: trying to prevent escalation in Russia-Ukraine war","publisher":"Euronews","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/22/ukraine-crisis-germany-scholz","claim":"Scholz said Russian nuclear threats were unacceptable and that Germany would continue supporting Ukraine while trying to prevent escalation beyond the Russia-Ukraine war.","locator":"paragraphs 653-658","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report quoting Scholz directly on nuclear rhetoric and escalation control.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Autumn 2022 crisis management.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["This is a reaction to Russian threats, not a German nuclear-policy decision.","It does not show command and control changes."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bund und Lander zu Ukraine-Fluchtlingen 'Es ist eine grosse Aufgabe'","publisher":"tagesschau.de","publication_date":"2022-03-17","url":"https://www.tagesschau.de/inland/bund-fluechtlinge-ukraine-101.html","claim":"Scholz said helping Ukrainian refugees was a major shared task and promised the states and municipalities financial support for reception and care.","locator":"lines 151-156","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous public-service reporting of Scholz's remarks and the federal-state response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Early-war humanitarian response.","ruler_attribution":"Direct personal attribution to Scholz.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian reception is not the same as conflict termination.","The statement is a policy commitment, not proof of later delivery."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Parlamentsprasidentinnen und -prasidenten der G7-Staaten verabschieden gemeinsame Abschlusserklarung","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/webarchiv/presse/pressemitteilungen/2022/pm-220916-g7ppk-abschlusserklaerung-910362","claim":"G7 parliamentary leaders condemned Russia's war against Ukraine, called for diplomacy and multilateral solutions, backed sanctions and support for Ukraine, and raised the prospect of a future peace conference grounded in Ukrainian sovereignty and territorial integrity.","locator":"lines 51-66","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary Bundestag-hosted multilateral declaration text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 multilateral peace framing.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect context for Germany's G7 presidency and Scholz government's diplomacy.","contrary_evidence":["Parliamentary declaration rather than executive decision.","Peace-conference language is aspirational."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"German Bundestag, 20th electoral term, Resolution","publisher":"Deutscher Bundestag","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://www.bundestag.de/dokumente/textarchiv/2022/kw08-sondersitzung-beschluss-englisch-883506","claim":"The Bundestag welcomed the government's active role in the united EU-NATO-G7 response, including sanctions and support for Ukraine, and called for additional political, economic, financial, humanitarian, and possible military aid.","locator":"resolution section around points 1-2 and subsequent text","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary parliamentary resolution text adopted immediately after the invasion.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Immediate 2022 war response and parliamentary support.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but attributable to the Scholz-led governing response.","contrary_evidence":["This supports the government response but does not prove operational effectiveness.","The resolution is collective, not personal."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.10"]}
